 SG_ SoftwareIdByte47 : 376|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" Vector__XXX

CM_ "Layouts per SAE J1939-71 (engine), J1939-75 (generator set) and J1939-21 (ACKM, Request), each checked against two public sources. Engine PGs: voltage-j1939 src/database.rs (github.com/EvanL1/voltage-j1939) and the Dafulai J1939 simulator manual (dafulaielectronics.com/DFLSJ1939BV1.pdf), the Hatz H50/E1 CAN protocol sheets (dsp.hatz.com) for rates. Generator PGs: Mecc Alte MxK CAN-Bus technical guide (meccalte.com/downloads/MxKs_CANBus_Tech_Guide_Eng.pdf) and Leroy-Somer D500 J1939 manual (leroy-somer.com/documentation_pdf/4971_en.pdf), with canboat (canboat.github.io/canboat) and isobus.net for the SPN numbers; GTACE bytes from canboat only. ACKM and Request: Wandfluh MKY45 J1939 specification and python-can-j1939 j1939_21.py. Byte n of a PG is bits 8(n-1)..8n-1 here. Unused bytes carry 0xFF; 0xFF-wide (not available) and 0xFE-wide (error) values decode to null. J1939-73 DM1/DM2, checked against the Wandfluh MKY45 J1939 specification and Open-SAE-J1939 DM1.c/DM2.c (github.com/DanielMartensson/Open-SAE-J1939): byte 1 lamps (bits 1-2 protect, 3-4 amber warning, 5-6 red stop, 7-8 MIL), byte 2 flash lamps, then 4-byte DTCs: SPN bits 1-16 in bytes 3-4, byte 5 bits 1-5 FMI and bits 6-8 SPN 17-19, byte 6 bits 1-7 occurrence count and bit 8 conversion method. 0 DTCs: 8 bytes, bytes 3-6 zero and 7-8 0xFF. 1 DTC: one 8-byte frame. 2+ DTCs: 2 + 4n bytes by transport protocol. The DBC holds two DTC slots: a shorter PG decodes what fits and leaves the rest null; a third DTC is not decoded. Every row above, DM1 and DM2 included, checked again against the SAE J1939DA extract the Equipment and Tool Institute ships in its J1939-84 tool (github.com/Equipment-and-Tool-Institute/j1939-84, j1939da-extract.csv and j1939da-slots.csv), the ISOBUS data dictionary (isobus.net, J1939DA PG pages), the Wireshark ISOBUS PGN table (epan/dissectors/data-isobus.c), the FMS-Standard v02.00 interface description and the Hatz H50/E1 CAN protocol sheets. The DA rates EEC1/EEC2 10 to 50 ms, HOURS and LFC on request and GTACE 100 ms; the bench sends what GenMsgCycleTime says.";
CM_ BU_ GENSET "Genset engine and generator ECU. J1939, preferred source address 0x80, arbitrary-address capable.";
CM_ BO_ 2364540032 "Electronic Engine Controller 1, PGN 61444, 100 ms (bench), priority 3. Byte 1 bits 1-4 torque mode and 5-8 high-resolution torque, byte 2 driver's demand, 3 actual torque, 4-5 speed, 6 controlling device's address, 7 bits 1-4 starter mode, 8 demand torque.";
CM_ BO_ 2364539776 "Electronic Engine Controller 2, PGN 61443, 50 ms, priority 3. Byte 1 pedal and road speed limit switches, 2 pedal position, 3 percent load, 4 remote pedal, 5 pedal 2, 6 limit and thermal management states, 7 maximum available torque, 8 pumping torque.";
CM_ BO_ 2566840192 "Electronic Engine Controller 3, PGN 65247, 250 ms. Byte 1 nominal friction torque, 2-3 desired operating speed, 4 asymmetry adjustment, 5 parasitic losses, 6-7 exhaust mass flow, 8 aftertreatment dew points.";
CM_ BO_ 2566844800 "Cruise Control/Vehicle Speed, PGN 65265, 100 ms. Byte 1 axle, parking brake and cruise pause switches, 2-3 wheel-based speed (not available: a genset goes nowhere), 4 cruise, brake and clutch switches, 5 cruise set/coast/resume/accelerate, 6 set speed, 7 bits 1-5 PTO governor state and 6-8 cruise states, 8 idle increment/decrement, test mode and shutdown override switches.";
CM_ BO_ 2348843257 "Torque/Speed Control 1, PGN 0, PDU1, received by the genset (destination 0x80 here; the id carries the tester's 0xF9 as source), priority 3, every 10 ms while a controller overrides the engine. Byte 1 bits 1-2 override mode (0 off, 1 speed, 2 torque, 3 speed/torque limit), 3-4 speed control conditions, 5-6 priority; 2-3 requested speed; 4 requested torque; 5 rate and purpose; 6 high-resolution torque; 8 counter and checksum.";
CM_ BO_ 2566843264 "Component Identification, PGN 65259, on request only, by transport: make, model, serial number and unit number, ASCII fields each ending in '*'.";
CM_ BO_ 2566844032 "Engine Temperature 1, PGN 65262, 1 s. Byte 1 coolant, byte 2 fuel, bytes 3-4 oil.";
CM_ BO_ 2566844288 "Engine Fluid Level/Pressure 1, PGN 65263, 500 ms. Byte 1 fuel delivery pressure, 3 oil level, 4 oil pressure, 7 coolant pressure, 8 coolant level.";
CM_ BO_ 2566846336 "Vehicle Electrical Power 1, PGN 65271, 1 s. Byte 1 net battery current, 2 alternator current, 3-4 alternator potential, 5-6 electrical potential.";
CM_ BO_ 2566841728 "Engine Hours, Revolutions, PGN 65253, on request per spec; the bench broadcasts it every 1 s. Bytes 1-4 hours, 5-8 revolutions.";
CM_ BO_ 2566842752 "Fuel Consumption (Liquid), PGN 65257, on request per spec; the bench broadcasts it every 1 s. Bytes 1-4 trip fuel, 5-8 total fuel used.";
CM_ BO_ 2566845056 "Fuel Economy (Liquid), PGN 65266, 100 ms. Bytes 1-2 fuel rate, 3-4 instantaneous economy, 7 throttle position.";
CM_ BO_ 2566845824 "Ambient Conditions, PGN 65269, 1 s. Byte 1 barometric pressure, 4-5 ambient air temp, 6 air inlet temp.";
CM_ BO_ 2566846080 "Inlet/Exhaust Conditions 1, PGN 65270, 500 ms. Byte 2 boost pressure, 3 intake manifold temp.";
CM_ BO_ 2365458048 "Generator Average Basic AC Quantities, PGN 65030, 100 ms, priority 3. Bytes 1-2 L-L V, 3-4 L-N V, 5-6 frequency, 7-8 current.";
CM_ BO_ 2365457280 "Generator Phase A Basic AC Quantities, PGN 65027, 100 ms. Same layout as GAAC; L-L is A-B.";
CM_ BO_ 2365456512 "Generator Phase B Basic AC Quantities, PGN 65024, 100 ms. Same layout as GAAC; L-L is B-C.";
CM_ BO_ 2365455744 "Generator Phase C Basic AC Quantities, PGN 65021, 100 ms. Same layout as GAAC; L-L is C-A.";
CM_ BO_ 2365457792 "Generator Total AC Power, PGN 65029, 100 ms, priority 3. Bytes 1-4 real power, 5-8 apparent power, both offset -2e9.";
CM_ BO_ 2365457536 "Generator Total AC Reactive Power, PGN 65028, 100 ms, priority 3. Bytes 1-4 reactive power (offset -2e9), 5-6 power factor (1/16384, offset -1), byte 7 bits 1-2 lagging (0 leading, 1 lagging).";
CM_ BO_ 2365454976 "Generator Total AC Energy, PGN 65018, 1 s, priority 3. Bytes 1-4 kWh export, 5-8 kWh import.";
CM_ BO_ 2565406592 "Acknowledgment, PGN 59392 (J1939-21 5.4.4), sent to the global address per the spec, to the requester by some stacks. Byte 1 control (0 ACK, 1 NACK, 2 access denied, 3 cannot respond), 2 group function, 5 address of the requester, 6-8 the PGN acknowledged.";
CM_ BO_ 2566834816 "Active diagnostic trouble codes, PGN 65226, 1 s.";
CM_ BO_ 2566835072 "Previously active diagnostic trouble codes, PGN 65227, on request only.";
CM_ BO_ 2566838912 "Software Identification, PGN 65242, on request only: RTS/CTS to a requester, BAM to a global request. The ASCII fields, each ending in '*', byte by byte.";

